   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to creating a sustainable energy loan program in the city of Binghamton",
    "basePrintNo": "S5867",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5867-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Binghamton, City of",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5867\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act in relation to creating a sustainable energy loan program in\nthe city of Binghamton\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nThe bill would authorize the City of Binghamton to establish a\nsustainable energy loan program to assist homeowners and businesses\nwithin the city of Binghamton in the installation of energy efficiency\nimprovements.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nSection one of the bill sets forth the legislative intent of the City\nof Binghamton to facilitate efforts of its residents and businesses to\nutilize energy more efficiently and utilize renewable energy sources\nto reduce carbon emissions and improve the environment.\n\nSection two of the bill establishes the City of Binghamton Sustainable\nEnergy Loan Program and authorized the City of Binghamton to use\nfederal grants to implement the program.\n\nThis section also provides that the borrower repay the city through an\nassessment on the real property where the sustainable energy loan was\napplied and that the assessment be included annually within the real\nproperty tax bill until repaid in full.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThis legislation will help lower energy costs, reduce greenhouse gas\nemissions and make energy audits and energy efficiency improvements\nmore affordable by offering a sustainable energy loan program to\nassist property owners within the city of Binghamton in the\ninstallation of energy efficiency improvements.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\n2009: New\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS :\n\nFederal funds will be used to capitalize the loan fund. The aggregate\namount of each sustainable energy loan provided by the city of\nBinghamton shall not exceed the actual cost of performing the energy\naudit, of installing energy efficiency improvements, including the\ncosts of necessary equipment and materials and installation costs, and\nof reasonable administrative costs.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
